            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\": \"Subordination, defeat, or the lowest and least significant position, often contrasted with the head which represents leadership and prominence.\",\"primary_basis\": [\"Deuteronomy 28:13\", \"Deuteronomy 28:44\"],\"alternatives\": [{\"meaning\": \"False prophets, lies, and spiritual deception, representing those who follow and lead others astray with falsehoods.\",\"basis\": [\"Isaiah 9:15\", \"Revelation 12:4\"],\"prominence\": \"common\"},{\"meaning\": \"Destructive power, venom, or demonic aftermath, particularly the trailing sting of judgment in apocalyptic imagery.\",\"basis\": [\"Revelation 9:10\", \"Revelation 9:19\"],\"prominence\": \"common\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\": true,\"confidence\": \"high\",\"notes\": \"The head-and-tail dichotomy is well established in the Old Testament covenant blessings and curses to denote rulers versus the subjugated. In prophetic literature, it takes on an ethical dimension distinguishing true leaders from lying prophets, while in apocalyptic literature, tails often carry the sting of judgment or represent the sweeping reach of demonic power.\"}",
